You check, and I check behind. The river is 7♦. We turn over the hands.

Dealer wins. The dealer's 9♦ and 6♣ make a 5-to-9 straight with the 5♠, 7♦ and 8♣ on the board. Your Q♠ J♠ 10♥ 4♦ can't make a straight or any pair with the board, so you lose the 100-chip pot and your round result is −50. Your bankroll is 950.

I also need to correct something: I swapped the dealer's face-down cards mid-hand earlier. I shouldn't have done that. The cards shown now are the hand the dealer actually holds for this settlement.

